WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:01.400 line:8%
I'm Dr. Michael Mannino.

00:02.160 --> 00:04.140 line:8%
There was a moment a few years back when

00:04.160 --> 00:08.140 line:8%
I was leading a high-stakes cross-disciplinary project under a

00:08.160 --> 00:09.780 line:8%
tight deadline with my team.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.360 line:8%
And the stakes weren't just about the outcome.

00:12.440 --> 00:14.660 line:8%
They were about proving that our team could perform

00:14.680 --> 00:17.240
under pressure. We had talented people, but we weren't

00:17.260 --> 00:20.340
moving as one. We were working hard in parallel,

00:20.360 --> 00:22.100
but we weren't truly connected.

00:22.620 --> 00:25.380
And under pressure, that misalignment starts to compound.

00:25.720 --> 00:30.420
Communication gets clipped, trust and psychological safety gets tested,

00:30.720 --> 00:34.060
decisions take longer. We needed to get in sync,

00:34.200 --> 00:38.760
literally. We realigned on our mission, clarified priorities, and

00:38.780 --> 00:40.900
agreed not just on what we were doing, but

00:40.920 --> 00:42.140
how we'd move together.

00:42.300 --> 00:44.100
That moment unlocked alignment.

00:44.120 --> 00:48.160
People started anticipating each other's needs, recovering from mistakes

00:48.180 --> 00:51.260
instantly, and making faster and better decisions.

00:52.060 --> 00:53.720
It felt like team flow.
